# apps/web build-time configuration. Vite inlines every
# `VITE_*` access at build, so this file documents the
# build-time toggles a contributor needs to set in their
# local `apps/web/.env` (gitignored — same convention as the
# workspace `.env`).

# -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Phase 1.20b — Web Push subscribe key.
#
# Public half of the VAPID keypair that `lakko-svc-push-gw`
# uses to encrypt outbound Web Push wakes (RFC 8291). The
# client passes this to `PushManager.subscribe({
# applicationServerKey })` so the browser-side push service
# (FCM endpoint on Chrome, Mozilla autopush on Firefox) binds
# the subscription to *our* server.
#
# Encoded as base64url-no-pad of the 65-byte uncompressed
# P-256 point. Must match the private half on the server
# (`LAKKO_WEBPUSH_VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY_PEM` in the workspace
# `.env`).
#
# Generate once via `npx web-push generate-vapid-keys`:
#
#     $ npx web-push generate-vapid-keys
#     =======================================
#     Public Key:
#     BL...           # ← this value
#
#     Private Key:
#     xZ...           # ← goes in workspace .env
#     =======================================
#
# Unset = the subscribe orchestrator is a no-op (clients
# fall back to foreground polling). Right posture for any
# contributor not actively iterating on push.
# VITE_LAKKO_WEBPUSH_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY_B64URL=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------
# SFU group-call endpoint (SFU multi-party arc).
#
# The Rust SFU's WebSocket origin (ws:// or wss://, no trailing
# path). The web client appends `/v1/connect` and offers the call JWT
# as a `lakko-sfu-token.<jwt>` WebSocket subprotocol. The SFU
# terminates WebSocket signaling + UDP media directly, so it is a
# SEPARATE deployment from the `/api/*` services nginx fronts — it
# does NOT ride the relative `/api` base the other clients use.
#
# Group calls (>2-member chats) route through this endpoint with
# SFrame end-to-end media encryption; 1×1 chats stay peer-to-peer
# and ignore it. Unset = the group-call button surfaces a clear
# "SFU endpoint not configured" error rather than dialing nothing
# (1×1 calls are unaffected).
#
# The SFU is a different origin, so the page's CSP `connect-src` must
# name it. `scripts/post-build.mjs` adds this value's origin to the
# `<meta>` CSP automatically; the production HEADER copy in
# `infra/nginx/sites-available/lakko.conf` is static and must carry
# the same origin (`wss://sfu.lakko.me` today) — post-build warns if
# it does not. Same for VITE_LAKKO_TRANSPARENCY_URL below.
# VITE_LAKKO_SFU_URL=wss://sfu.lakko.me

# -----------------------------------------------------------------
# KT-log S3c — transparency-log inclusion check.
#
# When the web client fetches a CONTACT's published identity from
# discovery, it ALSO consults the operator-signed, append-only
# transparency log to confirm that identity is committed by the
# public log — the equivocation-detection / gossip layer on top of
# the ADR-0016 supersession/pin gate (which stays the primary,
# fail-closed trust). The log check is ADDITIVE: it hard-fails only
# on a rollback (the log shrank — an unambiguous attack); an absent /
# unreachable / mismatch verdict is recorded + surfaced but does NOT
# block.
#
# BOTH vars must be set for the check to run; unset EITHER and the
# whole log check is OFF (the right posture for a contributor not
# iterating on transparency, or a deployment that has not provisioned
# the operator key).

# Transparency service base URL (https://…, no trailing path). The
# client appends `/transparency/{root,latest/:key,proof/:idx}`. This
# is a SEPARATE deployment from the `/api/*` services nginx fronts.
# Unset = log check OFF.
# VITE_LAKKO_TRANSPARENCY_URL=https://transparency.lakko.me

# Operator's Ed25519 verifying key, base64 (standard alphabet) of the
# 32-byte key. This is the trust anchor for every signed root and is
# PINNED OUT-OF-BAND at build time — the client NEVER trusts the
# `/transparency/operator-key` endpoint for verification, so a
# malicious serving tier cannot swap the operator key. Obtain it via
# a trusted channel (e.g. the project's signed release notes), NOT by
# curling the live endpoint. Unset / malformed / wrong-length = log
# check OFF.
# VITE_LAKKO_TRANSPARENCY_OPERATOR_KEY=

# Witness's Ed25519 verifying key, base64 (standard alphabet) of the
# 32-byte key (ADR-0020 split-view defence). PINNED OUT-OF-BAND at
# build time, like the operator key. When set, the client REQUIRES a
# valid witness co-signature over every fetched root (the operator
# cannot serve a root the independent witness has not co-signed) — a
# root without one is refused (fail-closed). Unset / malformed = the
# witness gate is OFF and the client keeps the operator-only posture
# (the transition fallback). The witness MUST run in a DIFFERENT trust
# domain from the operator for the guarantee to hold.
# VITE_LAKKO_TRANSPARENCY_WITNESS_KEY=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Donations page (`docs/ux/donations.md` section 3).
#
# The public half of the OFFLINE donations key, base64url without
# padding (32 bytes), as `lakko-donations keygen` / `just
# gen-donations-key` prints it. Every donation method, QR image hash
# and phone number discovery serves is signed by that key; the page
# shows only what verifies against this pin. Unset / malformed = the
# page shows "No way to donate is available" and asks the server
# nothing. Never take it from the server.
# VITE_LAKKO_DONATIONS_KEY=
